{
  "name": "ModuleTypeIsNamedByItsModule",
  "comment": "A module's type is named by its module (ruling 7, decision 752). A type's name is its\nnamespace read from a root, like a file path, with no search for a unique tail — a\nmodule's type drops `app.module.` and its `type.` folder. So app.module.window.type.window\nis named `window.window`, app.module.screen.type.screen.window is named `screen.window`,\nand bare `window` is nobody's name.",
  "step": [
